.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_BEGIN 3 2026-09-28 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_begin \- begin creating a new MPQ patch archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_begin(mpq_patch_s **patch, const char *base_archive, const char *output_patch);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a staged patch artifact at \fIoutput_patch\fP using an existing filesystem MPQ at \fIbase_archive\fP. The base is read-only and is never modified. On failure, a valid \fIpatch\fP output is set to NULL. Finish publishes the artifact; abort discards it. Embedded and MPQE base archives are unsupported. Full Blizzard patch-metadata compatibility and signing are not provided.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid arguments return LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST; unsupported archive formats return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. Opening, allocation, and I/O errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__patch_replace_data (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_remove (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_finish (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_abort (3)
